<urn:atm:triage:finding/FTQ-019>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FTQ-019" ;
  triage:title "console_break_requests_reload_without_terminate and console_close_requests_terminate missing #[serial] — OnceLock statics shared across parallel Windows CI tests (lifecycle_control.rs:298,309)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/lifecycle_control.rs:298,309 — two #[cfg(all(test, windows))] tests (console_break_requests_reload_without_terminate at line 298, console_close_requests_terminate at line 309) call install() which populates OnceLock<Arc<AtomicBool>> statics (TERMINATE, RELOAD, STATE_CHANGE at lines 247-249) on first call; all subsequent calls share the same Arcs. Both tests reset flags with set_terminate_for_test(false) / set_reload_for_test(false) then assert immediately. Without #[serial], parallel Windows CI execution allows one test's flag reset to clobber the other's assertion window — intermittent false-negatives on terminate_requested() or take_reload_requested(). Fix: add #[serial] to both Windows test functions; import serial_test::serial inside the windows_tests module. Note: quality-mgr reported this as FTQ-018 in S.3 QA-3 report; remapped to FTQ-019 to avoid collision with canonical FTQ-018 (tests.rs:183 35ms sleep race on feature/pS-s2-windows-ipc)." ;
  triage:category "FTQ" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-S" ;
